core: give libsystemd-core the RUNPATH that systemd's executables have

libsystemd-core-NNN.so needs libsystemd-shared-NNN.so from
/usr/lib/systemd but has no DT_RUNPATH. It still loads, because
/usr/lib/systemd/systemd loads the shared library first, but the
library's own dependency is unresolved on its face, so CPS's generated
library dependencies require a cap/elf/.../libsystemd-shared-NNN.so
capability that nothing provides. Linking it with the same install_rpath
as the executables makes the dependency resolve inside the package.

Not upstream. Canopa-specific packaging fix.

--- a/src/core/meson.build
+++ b/src/core/meson.build
@@ -197,6 +197,7 @@
         link_depends : libshared_sym_path,
         link_whole: libcore_static,
         link_with : libshared,
+        install_rpath : pkglibdir,
         install : true,
         install_dir : pkglibdir)
 
